# Staged by pack.py from reference/bmx.js so the preview ships with a renderer. Generated, not source
# — two copies of a parser in version control is how they drift.
editors/vscode/reference/

# Built by `burxt build render.bx -o bmxrender`, per tools/README.md. A 232K compiled binary that
# rebuilds in seconds does not belong in version control — and a binary is not evidence of the
# source it came from, which this project has written down elsewhere.
tools/bmxrender

# The PNGs live in docs/assets/examples/, which is where the site serves them from. A second copy
# beside the generator is the drift hazard, one directory over.
tools/*.png

# `npm install vscode-textmate vscode-oniguruma` — what the grammar tests need, installed the same way
# CI installs it. Untracked and unignored, it turned up in every `git status` after the first local run
# of `scopes.mjs`.
editors/vscode/node_modules/
